Root cause:
The bug was caused by the lack of validation for the vGPU DMA address before it was used in the host side, which could lead to the use of an invalid guest DMA address. This oversight could result in DMA faults and potentially cause the GPU to hang, as the DMA address was being updated by the vCPU thread without proper checks in place before being utilized by the QEMU UI thread. The patch introduced mechanisms to pin and unpin the DMA address, ensuring that it is validated before being sent to the hardware.
